 # Bitcoin-Backed USDC One-Loan System Architecture
 
+The [architecture guide](../guide/architecture.md) explains the system for readers. This record holds its exact purpose, binding, authority and boundaries.
+
 Source brief: [Technical Brief](../../technical-brief.md)
 
-## System Overview
-
-The product coordinates one borrower, one selected lender, Bitcoin collateral, and USDC settlement on Base. Its five domains separate agreement meaning, participant Bitcoin authority, Base value movement, verified observation and conditional fallback, and durable application coordination. The separation matters because each can report progress without acquiring another's authority: login is not a Vault unlock, an accepted command is not a chain fact, and a Base refund is not a confirmed Bitcoin recovery.
-
-Loan Terms And Commitments supplies the shared identity and immutable candidate binding. Participant Access And Loan Operations presents and persists the workspace and sends narrowly bound actions to participant Vaults. Bitcoin Authorization And Recovery constructs and validates fixed participant-authorized packages, while Base USDC Settlement And Funding controls its own funding, acceptance, repayment, claim, and refund transitions. Base Observation And Fallback Review qualifies named Base events and independently constrains optional `S` publication. A normal repayment lets the lender disclose `Y`; lender silence can lead to a Base refund and, only for an activated precommitted fallback loan, conditional `S` recovery. Either Bitcoin path becomes final only when the expected spend confirms.
-
-Each domain below is a complete reading destination; responsibility and contract links provide precise detail. Runtime topology, construction dependencies, and state/sequence views are separate derived perspectives in the [visual index](../visuals/index.html). They do not replace this written architecture. Existing approval-wording and fee/count discrepancies identified by the migration remain unresolved source issues; this documentation revision does not choose new behavior.
-
 ## Purpose And Binding
 
 The system coordinates a browsable lender-published one-loan offer, one atomic borrower reservation, Bitcoin collateral, and a Base USDC loan between one borrower and one selected lender. Publication is the lender's standing acceptance of the offer; reservation creates the canonical loan without a second lender approval. The selected lender separately retains explicit control of the later capital-funding action. V1 is not public or multi-lender matching, pooled capital, product custody, or automatic capital deployment.
 
+Unresolved source conflict: this record ("Publication is the lender's standing acceptance of the offer; reservation creates the canonical loan without a second lender approval"; Cross-Domain Boundaries: "no second lender approval"), [IFACE-003](./contracts/interfaces/iface-003-one-loan-offer-reservation-and-loan-binding.md) and [SCOPE-011](./contracts/scope/scope-011-public-multi-lender-pooling-custody-and-automatic-capital.md) ("no second lender approval"), and [SEL-012](../build/records/selections/sel-012-one-loan-offer-reservation-and-binding.md) ("no second lender-approval step") versus [SR-001](./domains/loan-terms-and-commitments/responsibilities/sr-001-loan-terms-offer-reservation-and-parameter-binding.md) ("Publication is standing lender approval of the proposed commercial values only"; "Neither publication nor reservation approves or commits final bound terms"; borrower and lender "each explicitly approve the same candidate version/hash through authenticated application authority") and [IFACE-001](./contracts/interfaces/iface-001-loan-terms-and-canonical-binding.md) ("The second matching approval and canonical agreement creation commit atomically"). Neither side is chosen here; the approval wording waits for the user's answer.
+
 Every domain identifies the same loan through one canonical `LoanTermsV1` value and `terms_hash`. The binding covers immutable participant references, the selected offer revision and reservation number, asset and amount terms, deadlines, loan-specific Bitcoin public keys, independently selected external Bitcoin destinations, Base protocol addresses and fixed settlement recipients, and the commitments to `X`, `Y`, and conditional `S`. `ProtocolDeploymentV1` separately binds environment-wide chain, contract, asset, Bitcoin-network, timing-policy, and upgrade-authority facts. Neither commitment is a wallet, signing key, source of funds, chain-state fact, or lifecycle action. A participant Vault payment account is a separate public source-of-funds identity; selecting it as a fresh loan's existing recipient field requires fresh approval and does not rewrite historical terms.
 
