+- Open question: [IFACE-001](../../contracts/interfaces/iface-001-loan-terms-and-canonical-binding.md) defines `borrower_participant_id` and `selected_lender_participant_id` as "Nonzero, random per-loan" references, while [SEL-012](../../../build/records/selections/sel-012-one-loan-offer-reservation-and-binding.md) rejects an alternative because "A new opaque random participant reference would duplicate the identity the application already has." Whether these describe different references is undecided.
+- Open question: [SR-001](responsibilities/sr-001-loan-terms-offer-reservation-and-parameter-binding.md) lists terms states `commercial_draft`, `awaiting_allocations`, `awaiting_final_approvals`, `committed`, `cancelled`, and `superseded`, while [STATE-002](../../contracts/states/state-002-canonical-loan-terms.md) names Commercial draft, Awaiting acceptances, Committed, Cancelled, and Superseded, with no separate awaiting-allocations state. Whether these are one lifecycle under different names is undecided.
+- Canonical encoding: the recorded rationale is interoperability and verifiability; divergent encodings or mixed immutable and deployment facts could bind signatures, manifests, and chain actions to different loans, or make a package impossible to reproduce. The exact encoding and accepted address spellings remain in [IFACE-001](../../contracts/interfaces/iface-001-loan-terms-and-canonical-binding.md).
+- Separating immutable loan facts (`LoanTermsV1`) from environment facts (`ProtocolDeploymentV1`) prevents different consumers from signing or processing different meanings under the same label.
+- Every consumer rejects an unsupported encoding, changed fingerprint, wrong chain/contract/asset/network, mixed environment, wrong key or destination, or dependent artifact that does not bind exactly; pre-activation amendment produces a later candidate/version and fresh dependent artifacts; cancellation ends that reservation and reopening requires a fresh loan identity. These rules prevent an apparently successful retry from reviving old approval or signing material.
+- An unresolved implementation question belongs in its existing ticket; a narrative or diagram cannot supply a missing approval.
